<edge source="В. И. СПИВАКОВ" target="МК «АЗОВСТАЛЬ»">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">В. И. Спиваков is involved in the study related to controlled rolling processes at МК «Азовсталь».</data>
</edge>
<edge source="МК «АЗОВСТАЛЬ»" target="Э. А. ОРЛОВ">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Э. А. Орлов is involved in the study related to controlled rolling processes at МК «Азовсталь».</data>
</edge>
<edge source="МК «АЗОВСТАЛЬ»" target="И. В. ГАНОШЕНКО">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">И. В. Ганошенко is involved in the study related to controlled rolling processes at МК «Азовсталь».</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="МАЛОПЕРЛИТНЫЕ СТАЛИ">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Контролируемая прокатка (КП) is applied primarily to малоперлитные стали to enhance their mechanical properties.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="НИТРИДО-И КАРБОНООБРАЗУЮЩИЕ ЭЛЕМЕНТЫ">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">КП often includes the presence of nitride- and carbide-forming elements to improve steel properties.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="ТМО">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Контролируемая прокатка (КП) is a specific case of the ТМО process used mainly for thick steel sheets.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="НИЗКОЛЕГИРОВАННЫЕ СТАЛИ">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Контролируемая прокатка (КП) is employed for producing low-alloy steels with enhanced qualities.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="ВЫСОКИЙ ТЕМПЕРАТУРНЫЙ РЕЖИМ">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Высокий температурный режим is part of the CP process to improve the rolling efficiency.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="НИЗКИЕ ТЕМПЕРАТУРЫ">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The CP process adjusts to low temperatures to optimize grain structure in steels.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="ФЕРРИТ">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Контролируемая прокатка (КП) aims to refine ferrous grains, enhancing mechanical properties of steel.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="КЛЕТЬ">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The rolling cage is essential equipment utilized during the controlled rolling process to shape the steel sheets.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="ПРОЧНОСТЬ">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling processes are designed to enhance the strength of the steel products manufactured.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="ВЯЗКОСТЬ">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The controlled rolling process seeks to improve the toughness and ductility of the steel produced.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="ТЕПЛОВАЯ ОБРАБОТКА">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The heat treatment that accompanies controlled rolling enhances the mechanical properties of the resulting steel.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="КПУО">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">КПУО и КП являются противоположными процессами прокатки, где КПУО использует более высокие температуры, чтобы достичь прочности.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="УО">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Низкотемпературная КП может сочетаться с УО для улучшения физических свойств проката.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="СТАН 3000">
  <data key="d6">11.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The Стан 3000 is a specialized milling machine employed in the controlled rolling process, specifically noted for its application in low-temperature rolling of strips (штрипсов). However, it is important to highlight that this mill lacks advanced cooling features, which may limit its efficiency in certain operations. Despite this limitation, its primary function within the controlled rolling framework remains significant, ensuring that materials are processed effectively under controlled conditions.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="СТАН 3600">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The 3600 mill allows for an advanced controlled rolling process including accelerated cooling.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="КП+УО">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The process КП serves as the basis for the КП+УО scheme, improving efficiency through integrated cooling methods.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП" target="ТЕМПЕРАТУРНЫЕ ПАРАМЕТРЫ">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Temperature parameters are critical in determining the controlled rolling process's performance.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="МАЛОПЕРЛИТНЫЕ СТАЛИ" target="ТЕМПЕРАТУРА ДЕФОРМАЦИИ">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Температура деформации должна соответствовать критериям, установленным для малоперлитных сталей</data>
</edge>
<edge source="МАЛОПЕРЛИТНЫЕ СТАЛИ" target="СЛИСТОВ">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Листы производят из малоперлитных сталей для повышения термостойкости</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ФЕРРИТ" target="АУСТЕНИТ">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The transformation of austenite to ferrite occurs during the controlled rolling process, affecting the final steel properties.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="NEPRYEVNOLITOGO METALLA" target="NOPTEMPERATURNY REGIM">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The low-temperature regime is crucial for the processes involved in continuous metal casting</data>
</edge>
<edge source="NOPTEMPERATURNY REGIM" target="T_H">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The regime must be maintained at T_H of 750-700 °C for proper metal processing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="NOPTEMPERATURNY REGIM" target="TEMPERATURE PROTOCOL">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The low-temperature protocol directly affects the metal’s cooling rates in controlled processes</data>
</edge>
<edge source="T_H" target="UOVT">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Accelerated cooling installation is crucial for managing temperature parameters during the cooling phase</data>
</edge>
<edge source="MANNESMAN-ROHREN" target="KONTROLIROVANNOY PROKATKI">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Mannesman-Rohren employs controlled rolling in their steel processing operations</data>
</edge>
<edge source="KONTROLIROVANNOY PROKATKI" target="VOEST-ALPINE">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Voest-Alpine utilizes controlled rolling processes to enhance their steel production</data>
</edge>
<edge source="KONTROLIROVANNOY PROKATKI" target="POSCO">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">POSCO implements techniques in controlled rolling in their steel manufacturing process</data>
</edge>
<edge source="KONTROLIROVANNOY PROKATKI" target="MK IM. 'ILIČA'">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">MK im. 'Iliča' employs controlled rolling processes for steel products</data>
</edge>
<edge source="KONTROLIROVANNOY PROKATKI" target="TOLSHINA PODKATA">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Thickness of material directly impacts controlled rolling parameters</data>
</edge>
<edge source="KONTROLIROVANNOY PROKATKI" target="TEXNOLOGICHESKIYE OPERACII">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Technological operations are fundamental to the controlled rolling process</data>
</edge>
<edge source="DURABILITY" target="PLASTICITY">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Durability of metals during rolling is influenced by their plasticity</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CHERNOVAYA KLETI" target="VYDERZHKA">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The roughing mill requires pauses for cooling between rolling passes</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CHISTOVAYA KLETI" target="RAVNOE PROKATKI">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The finishing mill contributes to achieving the required flatness of rolled materials</data>
</edge>
<edge source="НИЗКОТЕМПЕРАТУРНАЯ КП" target="ВЫСОКОТЕМПЕРАТУРНАЯ КП">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Высокотемпературная КП применяется для достижения производительности в низкотемпературной КП</data>
</edge>
<edge source="НИЗКОТЕМПЕРАТУРНАЯ КП" target="ПРОИЗВОДИТЕЛЬНОСТЬ">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Увеличение производительности связано с уменьшением времени выдержки раскатов в процессе низкотемпературной КП.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="НИЗКОТЕМПЕРАТУРНАЯ КП" target="ПРОЦЕСС КОМПЕНСАЦИОННОЙ ПРОКАТКИ">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Процесс КП включает в себя как низкотемпературные, так и высокотемпературные подходы для достижения необходимых свойств.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ВЫСОКОТЕМПЕРАТУРНАЯ КП" target="УСТАНОВКА УОВТ">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Установка УОВТ используется в процессе высокотемпературной КП для достижения заявленной температуры.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ТЕМПЕРАТУРА ДЕФОРМАЦИИ" target="ЗЕРНО ФЕРРИТА">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Температура деформации влияет на размер зерна феррита в стали</data>
</edge>
<edge source="СЛЯБЫ" target="ЧЕРНОВАЯ КЛЕТЬ">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Слябы проходят через черновую клеть для получения заданной формы и размеров.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="СЛЯБЫ" target="СОРТАТОПРОКАТ">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Сортатопркаты могут формироваться из слябов в ходе процесса прокатки.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ЧЕРНОВАЯ КЛЕТЬ" target="ЗАВЕРШАЮЩИЕ 3 ПРОХОДА">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Чередование завершающих проходов и работы черновой клети необходимо для получения требуемого профиля металла.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ПРОЦЕСС КОМПЕНСАЦИОННОЙ ПРОКАТКИ" target="ИСКУССТВЕННАЯ СХЕМА">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Искусственная схема позволяет лучше понять процесс компенсационной прокатки и настройки его параметров.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КПУО" target="УО">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">КПУО может включать ускоренное охлаждение как развивающий этап для улучшения характеристик раскатов.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КПУО" target="СТАН 3600">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Стан 3600 позволяет реализовать высокотемпературную прокатку с ускоренным охлаждением.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КПУО" target="УОВТ">
  <data key="d6">14.0</data>
  <data key="d7">КПУО (Коагуляция, Пептизация, Уплотнение и Осветление) представляет собой технологический процесс, который осуществляется на установке УОВТ (Установка Охлаждения Воды и Технологий). Данная установка позволяет эффективно контролировать охлаждение в процессе КПУО и обеспечивает оптимизацию всех этапов обработки. Использование установки УОВТ для выполнения процессов КПУО способствует улучшению качества и стабильности конечного продукта, за счет тщательной регуляции температурных режимов и условий пептизации. Таким образом, процесс КПУО и установка УОВТ взаимосвязаны, создавая синергетический эффект, который способствует повышению эффективности производственных операций.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КПУО" target="КОНСТРУКЦИОННАЯ ЛЕГИРОВАННАЯ СТАЛЬ">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Процесс КПУО улучшает характеристики конструкционной легированной стали</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КПУО" target="ПРОКАТКА">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Процесс прокатки связан с контролируемым процессом охлаждения для достижения желаемых механических свойств</data>
</edge>
<edge source="АЦ3" target="СТАЛЬ 09Г2ФБ">
  <data key="d6">5.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Температура АЦ3 имеет значение для стали 09Г2ФБ, определяя ее термическое поведение при прокатке.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="СМУО" target="СТАН 3600">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">СМУО используется на стане 3600 для обеспечения контролируемого охлаждения раскатов.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="СТАН 3600" target="ВЫСОКOTEMПЕРАТУРНАЯ КП">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The high-temperature controlled rolling process is optimally facilitated by the features of the 3600 mill.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="СТАН 3000" target="ТРУБНЫЕ СТАЛИ С КАРБОНИТРИДНЫМ УПРОЧНЕНИЕМ">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Стан 3000 предназначен для производства трубных сталей с карбонитридным упрочнением.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="СТАН 3000" target="КАЛИБРОВКА">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Калибровка стана 3000 важно для поддержания точности и качества производимых изделий.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ВЫДЕРЖКА" target="ТЕМПЕРАТУРЫ ОХЛАЖДЕНИЯ">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Правильная выдержка и контроль температур охлаждения обязательны для достижения желаемых механических свойств раскатов.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="МИКРОСТРУКТУРА" target="МАРТЕНСИТНАЯ ФАЗА">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Изменения в микроструктуре могут привести к образованию мартенситной фазы, что критично для определения прочности стали.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП+УО" target="КП+УО+КП">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The КП+УО process is a variant of the more complex КП+УО+КП scheme which integrates additional rolling steps.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП+УО" target="ОХЛАЖДЕНИЕ">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Cooling after rolling in the КП+УО process is necessary for achieving specific mechanical properties.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП+УО" target="ПАРАМЕТРЫ РЕЖИМОВ">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Operational parameters influence the efficiency and success of the КП+УО rolling process.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП+УО" target="ОБЖАТИЕ">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The level of obжатие in the КП+УО process is an important threshold for achieving the desired dimensions of rolled products.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП+УО+КП" target="ДЛИТЕЛЬНОСТЬ ПРОКАТКИ">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The duration of rolling in the КП+УО+КП scheme is less than other traditional rolling methods.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ОХЛАЖДЕНИЕ" target="УОВТ">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The cooling phase utilizes УОВТ to manage the temperature of the metal effectively after the rolling process.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КП 3600" target="ТЕМПЕРАТУРА НА-ГРЕВА СЛЯ-БОВ">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The КП 3600 process requires specific heating temperatures for effective slabs rolling.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="УОВТ" target="ДТУ">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Установка УОВТ используется для реализации процесса ДТУ на стане 3600</data>
</edge>
<edge source="УОВТ" target="РАСХОД ВОДЫ">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Установка УОВТ требует учета расхода воды для оптимизации процесса охлаждения</data>
</edge>
<edge source="УОВТ" target="СЕЛЬСИНОВЫЙ КОМАНД–АППАРАТ">
  <data key="d6">5.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Сельсиновый команд-аппарат контролирует операции памяти на установке</data>
</edge>
<edge source="УОВТ" target="ЛИСТ">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Лист обрабатывается на установке УОВТ в процессе охлаждения</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ДТУ" target="ТЕПЛОТЕХНИЧЕСКАЯ МОДЕЛЬ">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Модель разрабатывается на основе данных процесса ДТУ для оценки охлаждения</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ДТУ" target="РАСКАТ">
  <data key="d6">5.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Процесс раската связан с выполнением этапов ДТУ</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ДТУ" target="ПЛАВКИ">
  <data key="d6">5.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Количество плавок влияет на процесс ДТУ и его параметры</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ТЕПЛОТЕХНИЧЕСКАЯ МОДЕЛЬ" target="МЕХАНИЧЕСКИЕ СВОЙСТВА">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Теплотехническая модель помогает рассчитать механические свойства охлаждаемого проката</data>
</edge>
<edge source="МЕХАНИЧЕСКИЕ СВОЙСТВА" target="ТЕМПЕРАТУРЫ">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Температуры определяют механические свойства материалов после охлаждения</data>
</edge>
<edge source="РАСХОД ВОДЫ" target="РАСКАТ">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Расход воды имеет критическое значение для успешного осуществления процесса раската</data>
</edge>
<edge source="РАСХОД ВОДЫ" target="ТЕМПЕРАТУРА">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Температура влияет на количество расходуемой воды в процессе охлаждения</data>
</edge>
<edge source="РАСХОД ВОДЫ" target="ВОДА">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Вода используется в качестве основного материала для охлаждения в установках</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Д.А. ЛИТВИНЕНКО" target="В.И. ПОГОРЖЕЛЬСКИЙ">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Д.А. Литвиненко совместно с В.И. Погоржельским работал над контролируемым прокатом</data>
</edge>
<edge source="В.И. ПОГОРЖЕЛЬСКИЙ" target="Ю.И. МАТРОСОВ">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Ю.И. Матросов также был участником исследований под руководством В.И. Погоржельского</data>
</edge>
<edge source="НИР" target="ТЕРМОМЕХАНИЧЕСКОЕ УПРОЧНЕНИЕ">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Научно-исследовательская работа фокусируется на процессе термомеханического упрочнения</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КОНСТРУКЦИОННАЯ ЛЕГИРОВАННАЯ СТАЛЬ" target="ГРУББЛЕХ">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Грубблех производится из конструкционной легированной стали</data>
</edge>
<edge source="КОНСТРУКЦИОННАЯ ЛЕГИРОВАННАЯ СТАЛЬ" target="ПРОЦЕСС УПРОЧНЕНИЯ">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Процесс упрочнения применяется для обеспечения прочности конструкции из легированной стали</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="STEEL">
  <data key="d6">15.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling is an essential process employed in the production of steel, specifically aimed at refining the microstructure of the material to significantly enhance its mechanical properties. This technique involves subjecting the steel to deformation processes that optimize its characteristics, resulting in improved strength, toughness, and formability. Through controlled rolling, steel manufacturers can manipulate the grain structure of the steel, ensuring that the final product meets stringent industry standards for various applications. By integrating controlled rolling into the steel production process, manufacturers achieve a more versatile and high-performance material that can effectively meet the demands of diverse engineering and construction projects.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="T. TANAKA">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Dr. T. Tanaka has conducted research on the process of controlled rolling in steel production, highlighting its significance.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="AUSTENITE">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling affects the transformation and refinement of austenite grain structures into desired microstructures</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="HIGH TEMPERATURE">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">High temperature is crucial in controlled rolling as it aids in the recrystallization of austenite.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="LOW FINISHING TEMPERATURE">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Using a low finishing temperature in controlled rolling assists in achieving refined grain structures and improved mechanical properties.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="NOTCH TOUGHNESS">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The controlled rolling process aims to improve notch toughness by refining grain structures in the steel.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="BISRA GROUP">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The BISRA group researched and developed controlled rolling technology, paving the way for improved steel manufacturing practices.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="Γ-GRAIN STRUCTURE">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling affects the γ-grain structure by refining its size and promoting better transformation to the α-matrix.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="C—MN—NB FINE-GRAINED STEEL">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">C—Mn—Nb fine-grained steel is produced using controlled rolling processes to enhance its mechanical properties effectively.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="GAMMA">
  <data key="d6">15.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled Rolling and Gamma are two critical concepts in the field of steel processing and metallurgy. Controlled rolling utilizes specific deformation techniques aimed at influencing the gamma phase of steel. This process is particularly important as it promotes the transformation of the gamma phase into the alpha phase during the hot-working of steel. By effectively managing this phase transition, controlled rolling enhances the final properties of the steel, such as its strength, toughness, and overall performance.

The technique of controlled rolling particularly targets the deformation of the gamma phase, ensuring that the steel undergoes the desired transformations and achieves optimal characteristics. This approach is integral to modern steel manufacturing, as it not only improves material quality but also enables the production of steel that can meet the rigorous demands of various applications in construction, automotive, and other industries. Through the controlled manipulation of phase changes within the steel, the method ensures that end products possess enhanced mechanical properties, making them more suitable for their intended uses.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="UPPER BAINITE">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The controlled rolling process can affect the formation of upper bainite, depending on the temperature and strain rates used during processing.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="SUBGRAIN HARDENING">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling facilitates subgrain hardening through deformation processes, leading to improved steel strength.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="TANAKA">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Tanaka proposed key stages in controlled rolling, highlighting its importance for steel grain improvement.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="RECRYSTALLIZATION REGION">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The controlled rolling process operates within the recrystallization region to enhance mechanical properties by refining grains.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="BAINITIC STRUCTURE">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling helps avoid the development of a bainitic structure, promoting better toughness.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="DEFORMATION">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling involves the deformation of steel to create desired microstructures and improve mechanical properties</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="MICROSTRUCTURAL CHANGE">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling induces significant microstructural changes within steel, leading to enhanced mechanical properties.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="ROLLING">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling is a specific type of rolling process that aims to refine the grain structure of steel</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="MIXED GRAIN STRUCTURE">
  <data key="d6">5.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling can lead to the formation of mixed grain structures in steel</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="NIOBIUM">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Niobium is commonly added to steel during controlled rolling to enhance its mechanical properties through precipitation hardening</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="MECHANICAL PROPERTIES">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling significantly improves the mechanical properties of steel through processes like grain refinement and adjustment of transition temperature.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="DILATOMETRIC METHODS">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Dilatometric methods can be used to analyze the thermal and phase transitions occurring during the controlled rolling process, providing vital data on material behavior</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="STRAIN-INDUCED AR3 TEMPERATURE">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The strain-induced Ar3 temperature is a critical parameter that can be affected by the controlled rolling process, impacting subsequent phase transformations</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="YUTORI AND OGAWA">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Yutori and Ogawa conducted studies relevant to controlled rolling, influencing the understanding of microstructure development under this process</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="TRANSFORMED MICROSTRUCTURE">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The controlled rolling process leads to specific transformed microstructures that greatly affect the mechanical properties of the steel.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="NORMALIZED STEEL">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Normalized steel properties can be enhanced through controlled rolling processes, allowing for improved performance in various applications</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="QUENCHED AND TEMPERED STEEL">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Quenched and tempered steel processes can be utilized alongside controlled rolling to achieve desired mechanical characteristics</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="HOTPROLLED STRIP">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling is a technique applied during the production of hot-rolled strips to enhance the material's mechanical properties.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="GRAIN REFINEMENT">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling is a method explicitly aimed at achieving grain refinement to improve the mechanical properties of steel</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="ACICULAR FERRITE">
  <data key="d6">17.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling is a metallurgical process that significantly influences the microstructure of steel, primarily by facilitating the formation of acicular ferrite. This process is essential for producing acicular ferrite structures, which are known to enhance the toughness and strength of the final steel material. By carefully managing the rolling conditions, such as temperature and deformation rates, controlled rolling promotes the transformation of the steel's microstructure, resulting in the desirable acicular ferrite phase. This transformation not only improves mechanical properties but also ensures that the steel can perform reliably under various conditions. Overall, the interplay between controlled rolling and the development of acicular ferrite is crucial for manufacturing high-quality steel products with superior performance characteristics.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="RECRYSTALLIZATION">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Recrystallization can occur during controlled rolling, impacting the grain structure and mechanical properties of the steel</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="NON-RECRYSTALLIZATION REGION">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The non-recrystallization region is a critical parameter in controlled rolling that affects the final grain size and mechanical properties</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="FINISH ROLLING">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Finish rolling is a stage in the controlled rolling process that shapes and finalizes the properties of the steel</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="GRAIN SIZE">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling directly influences the grain size of the processed materials, enhancing mechanical properties</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="C-MN STEEL">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">C-Mn Steel is often processed using controlled rolling to enhance its mechanical properties for low-temperature applications.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="FINISH-ROLLING TEMPERATURE">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Finish-Rolling Temperature is a key parameter in the controlled rolling process that directly influences the final mechanical properties of the material.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="NORMALIZING">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling serves as an essential complementary process to normalizing for improved steel properties</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="QUENCHING">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling combined with quenching yields a much tougher material than either process alone</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="TEMPERING">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling followed by tempering provides a balance of hardness and toughness in steel</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="DEFORMATION BANDS">
  <data key="d6">15.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling is a process that significantly impacts the microstructural features of materials, particularly through the generation of deformation bands. These deformation bands act as effective grain boundaries, which play a crucial role in influencing the mechanical properties of the materials. The formation of these bands is integral to the outcomes of controlled rolling, as they enhance the material's characteristics and facilitate subsequent processing stages. By creating a refined microstructure that incorporates deformation bands, controlled rolling not only improves mechanical properties but also sets the groundwork for further manipulation and application of the material.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="SUPRAPOSITION">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The new thermomechanical treatments utilize supraposition to enhance the properties of steel</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="EFFECT OF FINISHING TEMPERATURE">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The finishing temperature has a direct impact on the outcome of controlled rolling processes, influencing mechanical properties</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="LOW-TEMPERATURE RANGE">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling at low temperatures enhances mechanical properties, leading to superior strength and toughness</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="FERRITE">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling is utilized to enhance the nucleation potential of ferrite by altering the microstructural formation during processing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="FINE-GRAINED POLYGONAL FERRITE">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling produces fine-grained polygonal ferrite through the application of specific deformation conditions</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="STRAIN-INDUCED PRECIPITATION">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling promotes strain-induced precipitation, which is crucial for strengthening the steel</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="MARTENSITE">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Controlled rolling can serve as a pre-treatment process before quenching to form martensite in steels</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="SOLUTE-DRAG EFFECT">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The solute-drag effect influences the enhancement of mechanical properties during controlled rolling by impeding dislocation motion</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="TRANSITION TEMPERATURE">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Transition temperature must be controlled during the rolling process to achieve the desired balance between hardening and toughness</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="DISLOCATION">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Dislocation movements during controlled rolling affect the material's strength and ductility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="CONTROLLED ROLLING" target="PROCESS VARIABLES">
