</edge>
<edge source="STEEL" target="NIOBIUM">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Niobium is added to steel to enhance its strength, specifically in relation to controlled rolling processes.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="STEEL" target="NB">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The addition of Nb to steel improves its mechanical properties, including toughness and strength, by enhancing the controlled rolling process.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="STEEL" target="AUSTENITE">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Steel can exist in an austenitic phase when heated to high temperatures, where it exhibits specific mechanical properties and structures</data>
</edge>
<edge source="STEEL" target="DYNAMIC RECOVERY">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Dynamic recovery is a process that occurs in steel during high-temperature deformation, affecting the material's flow stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="STEEL" target="DYNAMIC RECRYSTALLIZATION">
