<edge source="DEFORMATION" target="FINER GRAIN STRUCTURE">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The process of deformation is employed to achieve a finer grain structure in metals, significantly enhancing their strength and mechanical properties.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="DEFORMATION" target="ALPHA">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Deformation techniques significantly impact the microstructure, promoting the formation of desirable alpha grain structures through controlled processing conditions.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="DEFORMATION" target="FLOW STRESS">
  <data key="d6">7.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Flow stress affects the deformation behavior of steel, particularly during high-temperature processing.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="DEFORMATION" target="RECRYSTALLIZATION">
  <data key="d6">9.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Recrystallization occurs following the deformation process, as internal stresses in materials are relieved through structural changes.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="DEFORMATION" target="DEFORMATION BAND">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Deformation causes the formation of deformation bands within the material structure, demonstrating a direct relationship between process and microstructure</data>
