</edge>
<edge source="SEPARATIONS" target="MNS INCLUSION">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">MnS inclusions are a primary trigger for the initiation of separations in steel, influencing the brittleness of the material.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SEPARATIONS" target="UNIAXIAL YIELD STRESS">
  <data key="d6">5.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The uniaxial yield stress influences the likelihood of separation occurring within steel under stress conditions, as cracks develop when stress exceeds yield strength.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SEPARATIONS" target="DIMENSIONAL ANISOTROPY">
  <data key="d6">6.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Dimensional anisotropy contributes to the behavior of separations, leading to varying mechanical properties based on orientation.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SEPARATIONS" target="PLANE STRAIN">
  <data key="d6">5.0</data>
  <data key="d7">In plane strain conditions, the likelihood of separations occurring can be influenced by how stress distributes across the material.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SEPARATIONS" target="PLANE STRESS">
  <data key="d6">5.0</data>
  <data key="d7">In a plane stress scenario, separations can develop due to the differing stress states experienced by the material during loading.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SEPARATIONS" target="PROPAGATE">
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
